[
  {
    "category": "pattern",
    "content": "The skill-lifecycle workflow is highly efficient for end-to-end skill creation \u2014 it ran 4 phases in separate sessions (discover, draft, test, deploy) totaling ~17min. Pre-analyzing sessions before invoking the workflow (with specific pattern evidence) makes Phase 1 much faster."
  },
  {
    "category": "insight",
    "content": "12 coder gym sessions (150+ ops) are discovering work is 'already fixed' \u2014 gym Phase 2 (workflow variant) re-runs after Phase 1 fixes the issue. This is structural waste in gym infrastructure, not a behavioral skill gap."
  },
  {
    "category": "fix",
    "content": "Gym success_criteria.js that counts grep/find occurrences in raw transcript will match file content too, not just agent commands. Need to parse only toolCall arguments, not full transcript including tool responses."
  }
]

[
  {
    "category": "insight",
    "content": "`agents/` is a nested git repo; verify and diff agent files with `cd agents && git diff ...` because root-level git status/diff won\u2019t show changes inside the nested repository."
  }
]
